  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1256 AM CST Wed Nov 25 2026\n\nFriday through Tuesday:\n\nThe surface low is expected to push east on Friday and any rain\nover southeast WI is expected to end promptly Friday after \ndawn. A brief period of relative high pressure is then expected \nto move over the upper Great Lakes and skies may clear through \nthe late morning and afternoon. A mix of clouds and clear skies \nshould then persist overnight and through Saturday amid milder \ntemperatures in the upper 40s to around 50 as milder 925 to \n850mb temperatures linger in the wake of the departing low \npressure system to our east.\n\nSaturday late afternoon into Saturday night, the ECMWF and GFS \nboth depict a cold front moving through, though the evolution of\nrain on Sunday following this front is in question given model \ndifferences. The Euro amplifies a low pressure system that \ntracks through the Middle MS Valley region, while the GFS fails \nto form the low in favor of a narrow fgen drive band of rain \nover the eastern corn belt. The NBM brings 60% PoPs into \nsouthern WI Sunday morning, heavily favoring the Euro, though \nthese NBM PoPs may go down in subsequent runs given the \nuncertainty. If the Euro does verify, precipitation would be \nmostly rain, save for a few flakes mixing in Sunday night over \ncentral WI.\n\nHigh pressure would then take hold Monday and Tuesday amid \nabove normal temperatures in the mid to upper 40s.\n\nCMiller",
